   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "A remembered past event",
     "texto": [
      "**-았/었던** presents an action or experience as past and bounded, seen from the present: 가다 → **갔던 곳** (the place I went to), 좋다 → **좋았던 날** (the day that was good), 만나다 → **만났던 친구** (the friend I met). It does not necessarily mean the situation cannot be repeated."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Difference from -던 and -(으)ㄴ",
     "texto": [
      "**-던** usually highlights the memory of something habitual, ongoing or not presented as finished. **-았/었던** usually presents the action as completed. Context can make them overlap; it does not reduce to «it no longer exists». **먹은 음식** is a more neutral past form."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
